# ☕ Activity 1: Free Coffee Flyer

## 📌 Overview

For **Activity 1**, I created a flyer for a **Free Coffee event** held at **Arrupe Hall, Booth 7** on **August 6, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 3:00 PM**.

The main purpose of the flyer is to invite students and visitors to come, enjoy free coffee, and socialize. I wanted the design to feel **warm, welcoming, and relaxing**, similar to the experience of having coffee with friends.

---

## 🎨 Color Palette

I chose a **warm and neutral color palette**, mainly using **cream, brown, terracotta, and black**.

- 🤍 **Cream/Beige** – Used as the main background to give the flyer a soft, clean, and cozy appearance.
- 🤎 **Brown** – Represents coffee and creates a warm and comforting feeling.
- 🧡 **Terracotta/Dark Orange** – Used as an accent color, especially in the borders and bottom section, to make important information stand out.
- 🖤 **Black/Dark Brown** – Used for most of the text to provide good contrast and make the information easy to read.

I chose these colors because they are commonly associated with **coffee, warmth, comfort, and relaxation**. I also wanted the colors to complement each other without making the flyer look too overwhelming.

---

## ✍️ Fonts & Typography

I used a combination of **bold serif fonts** and a **simple sans-serif font**.

The **bold serif font** was used for the main heading, **"FREE COFFEE,"** because it immediately catches attention and gives the flyer a friendly but noticeable appearance. It also adds a slightly vintage and café-inspired feeling.

For the smaller information, I used a **cleaner and simpler font** so that the details would be easy to read, especially the coffee choices and event information.

I also used **different font sizes** to create visual hierarchy. This helps guide the viewer's attention in the following order:

**FREE COFFEE → Invitation Message → Coffee Choices → Event Details**

---

## ☕ Design Elements

The flyer includes several coffee-related illustrations and decorative elements, such as:

- ☕ Coffee cup illustration
- 🥛 Latte art
- 🪧 Small "Open" café sign
- 🤍 Heart illustrations
- 🏫 Ateneo de Davao University School of Nursing logo

The **large coffee cup at the bottom-right** serves as the main visual focal point. It makes the purpose of the flyer immediately recognizable even before the viewer reads all of the text.

The **Ateneo de Davao University School of Nursing logo** was placed at the top so viewers can easily identify the organization or group behind the activity.

---

## 📐 Layout

I organized the information so that the viewer's attention naturally moves through the flyer:

**Location & Event Title → "FREE COFFEE" → Invitation Message → Coffee Choices → Date & Time**

I also included enough **empty space** between the different sections to prevent the flyer from looking too crowded.

The **horizontal lines** help separate the sections and make the overall design more organized and visually balanced.

---

## 💡 Overall Concept

Overall, I wanted my flyer to have a **cozy, café-inspired aesthetic**.

My goal was not only to provide information about the activity but also to make people feel **interested, comfortable, and welcomed**. The warm colors, coffee illustrations, typography, and organized layout were chosen to create a relaxing café-like atmosphere.

The phrase:

> **"Come Sip, Connect and Smile!"**

represents the idea that the activity is not only about getting free coffee, but also about **socializing, building connections, and enjoying a relaxing moment with others**.

